Third-party software in tinfirm-runner-host
===========================================

tinfirm-runner-host, the Tinfirm runner host, is under the MIT licence: LICENSE, beside this
file. The part of it that comes from ee/runner in its repository, the tinfirm-bridge crate and
the runner host's modules of elastic runners, is under the Tinfirm Enterprise licence instead:
ee/LICENSE, beside this file. It is built from the Rust crates listed below, each under the
licence its entry names and gives in full, and statically linked with the Rust standard library
and, in the Linux builds, with musl libc (both at the end of this file).

This file is generated by cargo-about from runner/Cargo.lock (runner/about.toml, runner/about.hbs;
`make runner-licences`). Do not edit it by hand.

